y. With half her year spent in Canberra, reporting from Parliament House, and half her year in the sticks, she really does have a unique perspective. The Great Divide between city and country is only one subject that arises. The National Party talks about farmers, but what about those who live in regional towns? Her forensic focus in the nearby towns is on ordinary lives not often seen, and the conversations in this book are broad, national and at times international; immigration, transport, health, the NBN, globalization, and tariffs. Gabrielle also draws on her own observations about community.","subjectCategories":[{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Country life, australia","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-rusted-off-why-country-australia-is-fed-up-gabrielle-chan"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Australia, social conditions","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-rusted-off-why-country-australia-is-fed-up-gabrielle-chan"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Australia, politics and government","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-rusted-off-why-country-australia-is-fed-up-gabrielle-chan"}],"displaySummary":"With half her year spent in Canberra, reporting from Parliament House, and half her year in the sticks, she really does have a unique perspective. The Great Divide between city and country is only one subject that arises. The National Party talks about farmers, but what about those who live in regional towns? Her forensic focus in the nearby towns is on ordinary lives not often seen, and the conversations in this book are broad, national and at times international; immigration, transport, health, the NBN, globalization, and tariffs. Gabrielle also draws on her own observations about community.","primarySubject":"Politics & Government","primaryTopic":"Immigration, Refugees & Borderlands","subjectEvidence":{"primarySubject":"Politics & Government","confidenc